# 19. Testing Strategy

Build tests in layers.

## Unit tests

Test:

```text
Capability definition
Provider registration
Provider resolution
Model resolution
Configuration loading
Error handling
Unit conversion
```

## CoolProp adapter tests

Test representative calls such as:

```text
Water enthalpy(P,T)
Water entropy(P,T)
Water density(P,T)
```

Compare against known expected values with appropriate tolerances.

Do not rely exclusively on exact floating-point equality.

## Integration tests

Create a minimal graph:

```text
Water
  → uses_model
IAPWS Water
  → provider
CoolProp
```

Then resolve the model through the actual MonOSS database/relationship system and request a property.

The test must prove that:

```text
database graph
    ↓
model resolver
    ↓
provider registry
    ↓
CoolProp adapter
    ↓
property result
```

works end-to-end.

## Simulation test

Construct a minimal thermodynamic system using:

```text
Boiler
Turbine
Condenser
Pump
Water
```

and demonstrate that the turbine can request thermodynamic properties through the model system.

Do not build the complete Rankine-cycle solver as part of this feature unless required by the existing codebase. The goal is to establish the property architecture first.

